/chaosrack
# The old name of the binary. It was tracked before the rename and the rename
# carried it along, so a 37 MB ELF executable sat in the tree — and in every
# clone — for no reason.
/wasm-stuff

# chaosrack stlgen's output. Thirty-odd megabytes of generated geometry that any
# checkout can rebuild in a few seconds — and that the app does not need,
# since it generates the same models in the browser.
/docs/stl/

# Subagent worktrees — separate checkouts, never part of this tree.
.claude/worktrees/

# The other compiled binaries, tracked the same way /chaosrack once was:
# uitool 9.6 MB, uigolden 9.2 MB and probecmd 9.0 MB rode along in every
# clone. Removed from history 2026-09-03.
/uitool
/uigolden
/probecmd

# cmd/wasmmeters, if it is ever built without -o. The worker binary belongs
# in assets/metersworker, where `make metersworker` puts it.
/wasmmeters

# The animated gallery. `make gifs` writes it here and `make publish-gifs`
# puts it on the media branch, which Pages deploys beside the site: 96 MB of
# GIFs rode along in every clone, and every regeneration added another copy
# to the history. Removed from history 2026-09-27.
/docs/img/gif/
# The models' loops likewise (uitool portraits writes them; make publish-gifs).
/docs/img/model/*.gif

# `make onefile` writes this: the whole app in one HTML file, both runtimes
# inside it. It was tracked, 12.3 MB, and went 629 commits without being
# rebuilt while the site offered it as a download — it still said 66 models
# when the page said 73. Built on demand now, and not kept.
/chaosrack-standalone.html

# uitool monkey writes these where it is run when a walk fails. One was
# committed at the root with the first commit and stayed.
/monkey-fail-seed*.png

# The wasm builds, and the stamp of the sources each was built from. They
# were committed, by CI, on every push: 57 MB a time and 1.2 GB of history in
# seven weeks. CI publishes them as release assets now (pkg/wasmfetch); `make
# wasm`, tinywasm and metersworker write them here for a binary built here to
# carry. Removed from history 2026-11-12.
/assets/gowasm/chaosrack.wasm
/assets/gowasm/built-from.txt
/assets/tinywasm/chaosrack-tiny.wasm
/assets/tinywasm/built-from.txt
/assets/metersworker/meters.wasm
